peff-review ships its own PEFF-STYLE.md, 159 lines against the 197 here,
and the two have drifted. This commit does not touch it. The overlap is
the voice, which is genuinely shared, but the review copy has diverged
toward what a reviewer needs and merging them now would be a second
change wearing the same name.

COMPOSE.md is read by peff-commit-auto from a sibling directory, so the
paths inside it are written relative to COMPOSE.md rather than to the
skill reading it. That is a footgun worth remembering if a third caller
ever appears.
